## Testing Strategy

| Test Type | When to Run | Command |
|---|---|---|
| **TypeScript check** | **MANDATORY after every code change** | `npx tsc -b --noEmit` |
| Unit tests (touched files only) | During development, after each change | `npx vitest run src/path/to/changed.test.ts` |
| Product coverage (scoped) | During development / coverage fixes | `bash scripts/run-product-coverage-file.sh <file>` then `bash scripts/run-product-coverage-batch.sh <batch>` — see [`.cursor/rules/coverage-gates.mdc`](coverage-gates.mdc) |
| Demo coverage (scoped) | Demo lesson / demo-hub work | `bash scripts/run-demo-coverage-scope.sh <path>` — see [`.cursor/rules/coverage-gates.mdc`](coverage-gates.mdc) |
| Full unit test suite | **Only before merging** to `develop`, `release/*`, or `master` | `npx vitest run` |
| **Full product coverage gate** | **PR, merge to develop/release/master, or explicit user ask only** | `bash scripts/run-product-coverage-fast.sh` |
| **Full demo coverage gate** | **PR, merge to develop/release/master, or explicit user ask only** | `bash scripts/run-demo-coverage-full.sh` |
| Demo lesson E2E (one lesson) | After touching a specific lesson | `bash scripts/run-demo-e2e.sh <lesson-id>` |
| E2E tests (Playwright, full) | **Only before merging** to `develop`, `release/*`, or `master` | `npx playwright test --reporter=list` |
| GraphQL Phase 8 E2E sweep (19 lessons + gql110) | Before merging GraphQL demo work to `develop` | `./scripts/phase8-gql-e2e-sweep.sh` |
| Demo lesson (wrapper only) | Before marking lesson done | [`demo-lesson-done-checklist.md`](../../docs/guides/demo-lesson-done-checklist.md) — 5 items; wrappers excluded from 90% gate |
| **gRPC dev loop** | During gRPC feature work (every edit batch) | [`grpc-dev-loop.md`](../../docs/guides/grpc-dev-loop.md) — `npm run test:grpc:dev` or scoped vitest |
| **gRPC fast phase gate** | Sub-phase checkpoint before user verify | `npm run test:grpc:fast -- 11h` (skips regression chain) |
| **gRPC full phase gate** | Sub-phase sign-off / merge to `develop` only | `npm run test:grpc:phase11h` (full chain) |

### Dual-track builds (Standard vs Learning Hub)

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| Normal dev (demo on) | `npm run dev` |
| Prod-slim dev (no Demo Hub) | `npm run dev:prod-slim` |
| Web build — Standard | `npm run build:prod` (`VITE_ENABLE_DEMO_HUB=false`) |
| Web build — Learning Hub | `npm run build:demo` |
| Desktop — Standard | `npm run tauri:build:prod` |
| Desktop — Learning Hub | `npm run tauri:build:demo` |
| Unit tests — product only | `npm run test:product` |
| Unit tests — demo lessons | `npm run test:demo` |

**Demo package:** `@redfireforge/demo-hub` lives in `packages/demo-hub/` (Phase 7 monorepo extraction, 2026-06-26). See `packages/demo-hub/README.md` and `docs/plan/feature/separate-demo/separate-demo-codebase-plan.md`. gRPC lesson GRPC-24 (Workflow Runner & Results) helpers: `packages/demo-hub/src/lessons/protocols/grpc-workflow-runner-{helpers,steps}.ts`.

Product PRs that do **not** touch `packages/demo-hub/` or demo E2E specs are **not** required to run demo E2E or `test:demo`. Demo lesson work uses the [5-item done checklist](../../docs/guides/demo-lesson-done-checklist.md).

### Rules
- **Do not use `docs/plan/Dont-Remove-This-File.txt` as agent instructions** — it is the user's personal scratch file only. For gRPC dev/test tiers see [`grpc-dev-loop.md`](../../docs/guides/grpc-dev-loop.md) and [`.cursor/rules/grpc-dev-loop.mdc`](grpc-dev-loop.mdc).
- **Use shared test factories** — Import `makeScenario`, `makeResult`, `makeConfig` from `src/test-utils/factories.ts` instead of defining local factory functions in each test file. Wrap with thin local aliases if you need different defaults (e.g. `const makeScenario = (id) => _makeScenario({ id })`).
- **CRITICAL: Always run `npx tsc -b --noEmit` after making code changes.** This is NOT optional. The `-b` flag is required because the root `tsconfig.json` uses project references (`"files": []`); without `-b`, tsc checks nothing. Vitest and Playwright do NOT type-check source files — only `tsc` catches missing properties, bad imports, and type mismatches. Skipping this step causes Tauri build failures that are expensive to debug later. Run it after every batch of edits, not just before merging.
- **Do NOT run full coverage gates during iteration** — no `run-product-coverage-fast.sh`, `run-demo-coverage-full.sh`, or full-suite `test:demo:coverage` / `test:product:coverage` except when opening a PR, merging to `develop`/`release/*`/`master`, or the user explicitly asks. Use scoped scripts in [`.cursor/rules/coverage-gates.mdc`](coverage-gates.mdc).
- **During development, only run unit tests for the files you touched** — do NOT run the full test suite. Use `npx vitest run src/path/to/file.test.ts` to target specific test files.
- **Do NOT run full gRPC phase regression chains during iteration** — use `npm run test:grpc:fast -- <phase-id>` for checkpoints; full `test:grpc:phase*` only at sign-off. See [`grpc-dev-loop.md`](../../docs/guides/grpc-dev-loop.md).
- **Do NOT run E2E tests during regular feature development** — they are slow and only needed at merge gates.
- **Full test suite and E2E tests are ONLY run before merging** to `develop`, `release/*`, or `master`.
- During development, rely on `tsc -b --noEmit` + scoped unit tests for fast feedback.
- E2E tests require the dev server running on port 5173 (`npm run dev`).
- Target >90% code coverage on all four metrics (statements, branches, functions, lines).
- **Demo lesson wrappers** (`protocols/graphql-*.ts`, `ws-*.ts`, `sse-*.ts`, `kafka-*.ts`) are **excluded from the coverage denominator** — use the [5-item done checklist](../../docs/guides/demo-lesson-done-checklist.md) instead. Lesson **helpers** and demo player core remain at the full bar.

## Pre-Commit Hooks (Automated)

A husky pre-commit hook is configured to automatically run before every `git commit`:
1. `npx tsc -b --noEmit` — blocks commit if type errors exist
2. `npx lint-staged` — runs ESLint on staged `.ts`/`.tsx` files

This means **no commit can enter git with type errors**. If the hook blocks your commit, fix the errors first — do NOT bypass with `--no-verify`.

## Validation Operator UI/UX Reference

All 12 implementation phases (P0–P9.3) of the validation operator feature are **completed**. See `docs/plan/validation-operator-gap-analysis.md` for the full gap analysis, module architecture, and competitive benchmarks. The interactive HTML mockup at `docs/mockups/validation-operators-visual-mapper.html` remains the reference for UI/UX conventions:

- **Color scheme**: green (equality), amber (comparison), purple (string ops), teal (type checks), red (boolean), gray (existence/null), blue (set membership)
- **Operator pill placement**: inline on target tree nodes between the arrow (←) and source reference
- **Inline value editors**: appear next to operator pills when the operator requires a value; hidden for no-value operators (is_true, exists, is_null, type checks)
- **Array assertion rows**: render directly below array nodes with inline operator select, value input, edit, and remove controls
- **Operator picker dropdown**: categorized, searchable, with icon + name + description per operator
- **Right-click context menu**: quick assertion setup on target nodes
- **Code editor mode**: DSL syntax with syntax highlighting, autocomplete, and inline errors in the bottom dock
- **Validation stage**: per-node pass/fail badges (✓/✗), canvas line coloring (red for failed), footer aggregation, filter by status
- **Rules summary table**: bottom dock with operator column, status column, and color-coded operator pills

The UI must be **professional, clean, and user-friendly** — matching the dark theme tokens in `src/styles/data-mapper.css`. Avoid emoji-first labels; use symbols and structured typography. Every interactive element must have hover states, focus indicators, and appropriate `aria-label` attributes.

